@page "/about"
@layout Paycrest.Components.Layout.PublicLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>@L["About WageHarbor · Our mission"]</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="WageHarbor's mission: help every small business pay its people correctly and on time, with payroll and HR software at about a quarter of the usual price, free for one employee." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.wageharbor.com/about" />
</HeadContent>

<article class="prose">
    <h1>@L["Pay people right, and on time"]</h1>
    <p class="prose-sub">@L["Why we built WageHarbor."]</p>

    <blockquote>@L["“Give the worker his wages before his sweat dries.”"]<br /><small class="text-muted" style="font-family:inherit;font-size:.9rem">@L["Prophet Muhammad ﷺ · Sunan Ibn Majah 2443"]</small></blockquote>

    <p>@L["Fourteen centuries ago, that teaching made a simple point that every business owner still feels today: when someone has done the work, they have earned their pay, and holding it back is a wrong. Payday isn't paperwork. It's rent, groceries and peace of mind for the people who keep a business running."]</p>

    <p>@L["Yet for many small businesses, payroll is the hardest part of having a team. Software is expensive, tax rules change every year, and employees wait on HR just to see a pay stub. Mistakes and delays land on the people who can least afford them."]</p>

    <h2>@L["What WageHarbor does"]</h2>
    <p>@L["WageHarbor gives a small business the tools a large one takes for granted:"]</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>@L["Correct pay:"]</strong> @L["federal, Social Security, Medicare, state and unemployment taxes are calculated for every paycheck, with overtime and time off built in."]</li>
        <li><strong>@L["On-time pay:"]</strong> @L["a clear calculate → approve → pay flow, with a direct-deposit file ready for your bank."]</li>
        <li><strong>@L["Open pay:"]</strong> @L["every employee can see, print and save their own pay stubs and balances, any time."]</li>
        <li><strong>@L["Private pay:"]</strong> @L["each company's data is kept apart, and sensitive numbers are encrypted."]</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>@L["What we believe"]</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>@L["Fairness is practical."]</strong> @L["Paying correctly and promptly is the most concrete way a business shows respect for its people."]</li>
        <li><strong>@L["Small businesses deserve good tools."]</strong> @L["That's why WageHarbor costs about a quarter of similar apps, and nothing if you have one person on payroll. We're here to serve, not to squeeze: there are no ads, we never sell your data, and we charge only what it takes to run the service well."]</li>
        <li><strong>@L["Trust is earned with honesty."]</strong> @L["We tell you what WageHarbor does and doesn't do. For example, it calculates payroll taxes but you file them, and we'll keep it that clear."]</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="prose-cta">
        <p>@L["Ready to run your first payroll?"]</p>
        <div class="d-flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
            <a href="Account/Register" class="btn btn-primary">@L["Register your company"]</a>
            <a href="help/company" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">@L["Read the company guide"]</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
